    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-10-07T07:00:01.907Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":13},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_taurus-has-joined-xdc-network-as-an-institutional-activity-7513493321948774402-HQGP","text":"Taurus has joined XDC Network as an institutional validator.\n\nBy operating a validator node, Taurus will participate directly in XDC Network’s consensus infrastructure, helping validate transactions and support the security and resilience of the network. \n\nLearn more: https://lnkd.in/eWD6YHkT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_taurus-has-joined-xdc-network-as-an-institutional-activity-7513493321948774402-HQGP"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-10-06T06:24:01.050Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":26},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_tomorrow-at-digital-assets-week-london-kylie-activity-7513121870792015873-y7ih","text":"Tomorrow at Digital Assets Week London, Kylie Poole, MBA, Sales Director UK & Nordics at Taurus, will join a panel tackling one of the central questions for institutions entering digital assets: how should custody be structured?\n\nDigital Asset Custody: Regulated Custodian? Self-Custody? Build? Buy?\n\nThe discussion will look at the different custody models available to institutions and what each means for control, compliance, cost, security, and counterparty risk.\n\nKylie will be joined by Simon Barnby (CMO, Archax), Jasper Williams (Digital Custody Product, State Street), Jacques Boschung (CEO, Halborn), and Daniel Elsawey (Global Head of Partnerships, Bitpanda Enterprise),\n\n🔹 Wednesday, October 7\n🔹 10:50 AM\n\nMore details here: https://daweek.org/london/","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_tomorrow-at-digital-assets-week-london-kylie-activity-7513121870792015873-y7ih"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-10-05T13:02:15.091Z","headline":"","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":47},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_a-strong-sibos-week-in-miami-made-even-better-activity-7512859701798129665-uiAF","text":"A strong Sibos week in Miami, made even better by an evening with clients and partners.🌴\n\nTogether with Stellar Development Foundation, we co-hosted a private dinner with leaders from banking and digital assets, with Lamine Brahimi, CFA, Milena Kohlhofer, Bashir Kazour, Zachary Bender, and Bruno Reis joining from Taurus.\n\nAs we continue to expand in the U.S., we’re seeing growing engagement from financial institutions across the market. The evening was a great opportunity to reconnect with clients and partners and spend time with many of the institutions driving that interest.\n\nThank you to the Stellar Development Foundation and everyone who joined us!🤝","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_a-strong-sibos-week-in-miami-made-even-better-activity-7512859701798129665-uiAF"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-10-01T11:37:11.516Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":43},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_this-week-in-zurich-ryan-s-security-engineer-activity-7511388744394973184-G0ux","text":"This week in Zurich, Ryan S., Security Engineer at Taurus, joined OpenZeppelin and CMTA for a discussion on confidentiality in regulated onchain markets, hosted by Lenz & Staehelin.\n\nAs more financial activity moves onchain, institutions need to protect sensitive information while keeping the right controls in place.\n\nRyan showed how CMTAT-Confidential combines CMTAT Solidity with ERC-7984 to:\n◆ Encrypt holder balances\n◆ Protect transfer, mint, and burn amounts\n◆ Let issuers choose whether to disclose total supply\n◆ Keep compliance controls operating at the address level\n◆ Give holders, auditors, and regulators permissioned access to encrypted values\n\nThis approach helps financial institutions add confidentiality onchain without changing the controls around the asset.\n\nThank you to OpenZeppelin, CMTA, and Lenz & Staehelin, and everyone who joined the discussion in Zurich! 🙌 ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_this-week-in-zurich-ryan-s-security-engineer-activity-7511388744394973184-G0ux"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-09-30T06:19:02.541Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":32},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_sibos-miami-is-where-some-of-the-biggest-activity-7510946291565342720-Azq6","text":"Sibos Miami is where some of the biggest conversations in financial infrastructure are happening this week.\n\nTokenized assets, custody, settlement, and interoperability are all on the agenda, and the Taurus team is there throughout the event.\n\nIf you’re attending, connect with:\n🔹 Lamine Brahimi, CFA, Co-Founder & Managing Partner\n🔹 Milena Kohlhofer, Strategic Partnerships Executive\n🔹 Zachary Bender, Senior Sales Director\n🔹 Bashir Kazour, Managing Director\n🔹 Bruno Reis, Regional Head, Brazil and South America\n\n👉 Book a meeting here: https://lnkd.in/erv8ha7k","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_sibos-miami-is-where-some-of-the-biggest-activity-7510946291565342720-Azq6"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-09-28T13:27:22.231Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":13},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_chainlink-ccip-20-is-now-live-taurus-is-activity-7510329308142546944-w_J5","text":"Chainlink CCIP 2.0 is now live.\n\nTaurus is pleased to be a strategic launch partner, supporting more secure and scalable interoperability for institutional digital assets.\n\nAs Lamine Brahimi, CFA, Co-Founder and Managing Partner at Taurus, said:\n\n\"Chainlink CCIP is a key standard for how digital assets are managed and distributed across global markets, enabling assets to move seamlessly between blockchains while maintaining institutional security, compliance, and operational controls.\"\n\nLearn more: https://lnkd.in/eCk6GE-4\n\nChainlink Labs","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_chainlink-ccip-20-is-now-live-taurus-is-activity-7510329308142546944-w_J5"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-09-28T12:04:50.371Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":76},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_tokenised-money-market-funds-design-considerations-activity-7510308538540281856-tsxV","text":"Tokenised money market funds are the largest and fastest-growing category of tokenised real-world assets.\n\nYet the market has not converged on a single design. Issuers have made materially different contract choices because each fund has its own valuation and income conventions.\n\nA CNAV fund and a VNAV fund require different structures. Accumulating and distributing share classes differ again.  \n\nOur new whitepaper explains how those fund conventions translate into smart contract design, so financial institutions can assess the choices in the right order: start with the fund, then choose the contract.\n\n📘 In the whitepaper, we cover:\n\n🔹 Which fund conventions determine the design\n🔹 The four ways value can reach the holder\n🔹 The four smart contract families used in practice\n🔹 How to identify the structure that fits the fund\n🔹 How selected tokenised funds are structured today\n🔹 What financial institutions need to consider around pricing, 24/7 dealing, distributions, collateral, costs, and multi-chain supply\n\n📥 Download the whitepaper here: https://lnkd.in/e3kw_R72","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_tokenised-money-market-funds-design-considerations-activity-7510308538540281856-tsxV"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-09-25T07:23:38.571Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":38},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_next-week-in-miami-milena-kohlhofer-our-activity-7509150609481183232-nIOJ","text":"Next week in Miami, Milena Kohlhofer, our Strategic Partnerships Executive, will be speaking at Sibos on the infrastructure behind intraday repo.\n\nTogether with Rene Michau from Standard Chartered, Jonathan Chambers from U.S. Bank, Craig Perrin from Zodia Custody, and Philippe Redaelli from Kaiko, she’ll explore the infrastructure, settlement, liquidity, and collateral requirements behind intraday repo.\n\nNatasha Benson of Ownera will moderate the session.\n\n📅 Monday, September 28 at 9:00 AM ET\n\nIf you are attending, join us for the discussion and meet the Taurus team.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_next-week-in-miami-milena-kohlhofer-our-activity-7509150609481183232-nIOJ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-09-24T07:25:15.804Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":40},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_over-the-last-12-months-digital-assets-activity-7508788629440339968-moP1","text":"\"Over the last 12 months, digital assets have moved from being kind of a niche initiative to being a C-level agenda point.\"\n\nIn his recent interview with FinTech Magazine, Lamine Brahimi, CFA, Co-founder and Managing Partner at Taurus, discusses our integration with Swift’s blockchain-based shared ledger, the opportunity for Swift members, and how financial institutions can use it to support tokenized deposits and 24/7 cross-border payments. \n\n👉 Read the full interview: https://lnkd.in/eNGRmxk8","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_over-the-last-12-months-digital-assets-activity-7508788629440339968-moP1"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa"},"datePublished":"2026-09-23T06:53:18.466Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":30},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_this-week-security-and-risk-leaders-are-activity-7508418199676338176-4I7R","text":"This week, security and risk leaders are gathering in London for the Gartner Security & Risk Management Summit.\n\nMarc-Antoine Künzi, our CSO, will be there meeting CISOs and cybersecurity leaders to discuss the security and operational requirements of institutional digital asset custody, from key management and operational resilience to post-quantum readiness.\n\n📍 ExCeL London\n📅 September 22–24\n\nMore information:\nhttps://lnkd.in/d_dyEcg","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/taurus-sa_this-week-security-and-risk-leaders-are-activity-7508418199676338176-4I7R"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"Taurus SA","url":"https://ch.linkedin.com/company/taurus-sa","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"Place Ruth-Bösiger 6","addressLocality":"Geneva","addressRegion":"Geneva","postalCode":"1201","addressCountry":"CH"},"description":"Taurus is the #1 independent player and a global-leader in enterprise-grade digital asset infrastructure with roots in Switzerland.\n\n1️⃣ Market leadership: Taurus has \u003E50% market share in its home market in Switzerland, the most competitive in the world. Globally, Taurus is entrusted by the full spectrum of financial institutions - systemic banks, investment banks, crypto banks, private banks, universal banks - financial market infrastructure providers and core banking systems. In production.\n\n2️⃣ Product leadership: Taurus has developed the most advanced and most complete digital asset platform in the industry which goes “way beyond” crypto-currency custody. No one else besides Taurus, is able to empower financial institutions to issue/onboard, manage, and book “any type” of tokenised securities and digital currencies. On any standard. With the same platform.\n\n3️⃣ Technology leadership: Taurus masters the full technology stack and 70% of our staff is made of engineers. We believe this is a core capability and a strong hedge against tech disruptions in an industry that is young and moving fast. The products our clients use are 100% built by Taurus and are at the forefront of what exists in the market with several patent-pending inventions. Anticipating protocol upgrades, adding \"complex\" new protocols, new signature curves or strengthening HSM-security, operating nodes+indexing is totally controlled by our engineering teams. This makes us future-proof, execute fast and a long-term, partner to our clients. \n\nTaurus is growing fast and always looking for talents. Contact us at https://www.taurusgroup.ch\n\nFor other business enquiries: contact@taurusgroup.ch","numberOfEmployees":{"value":122,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/C560BAQFL34RV8D0HKA/company-logo_200_200/company-logo_200_200/0/1630501170331/taurus_sa_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=M5VFACUDdlCE_dRdzyWtm1kGUYd1jJS0jLOeOdyOHXg","description":"Taurus SA","@type":"ImageObject"},"slogan":"#1 platform for custody and tokenisation of ANY digital asset: cryptoassets, tokenised assets, digital currencies","sameAs":"https://www.taurushq.com/book/"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
