  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">This week in Zurich, <a class="link" href="https://ch.linkedin.com/in/ryan-sge?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Ryan S.</a>, Security Engineer at Taurus, joined <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/openzeppelin?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>OpenZeppelin</a> and <a class="link" href="https://ch.linkedin.com/company/cmta-ch?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>CMTA</a> for a discussion on confidentiality in regulated onchain markets, hosted by <a class="link" href="https://ch.linkedin.com/company/lenz-&amp;-staehelin?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Lenz &amp; Staehelin</a>.

As more financial activity moves onchain, institutions need to protect sensitive information while keeping the right controls in place.

Ryan showed how CMTAT-Confidential combines CMTAT Solidity with ERC-7984 to:
◆ Encrypt holder balances
◆ Protect transfer, mint, and burn amounts
◆ Let issuers choose whether to disclose total supply
◆ Keep compliance controls operating at the address level
◆ Give holders, auditors, and regulators permissioned access to encrypted values

This approach helps financial institutions add confidentiality onchain without changing the controls around the asset.

Thank you to <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/openzeppelin?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>OpenZeppelin</a>, <a class="link" href="https://ch.linkedin.com/company/cmta-ch?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>CMTA</a>, and <a class="link" href="https://ch.linkedin.com/company/lenz-&amp;-staehelin?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Lenz &amp; Staehelin</a>, and everyone who joined the discussion in Zurich! 🙌 </p>
<!---->  </div>



        

        
            
      
    
    
    

