  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Tokenised money market funds are the largest and fastest-growing category of tokenised real-world assets.

Yet the market has not converged on a single design. Issuers have made materially different contract choices because each fund has its own valuation and income conventions.

A CNAV fund and a VNAV fund require different structures. Accumulating and distributing share classes differ again.  

Our new whitepaper explains how those fund conventions translate into smart contract design, so financial institutions can assess the choices in the right order: start with the fund, then choose the contract.

📘 In the whitepaper, we cover:

🔹 Which fund conventions determine the design
🔹 The four ways value can reach the holder
🔹 The four smart contract families used in practice
🔹 How to identify the structure that fits the fund
🔹 How selected tokenised funds are structured today
🔹 What financial institutions need to consider around pricing, 24/7 dealing, distributions, collateral, costs, and multi-chain supply

📥 Download the whitepaper here: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/e3kw_R72?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/e3kw_R72</a></p>
